# Developer settings for running the app from source. Copy this file to .env and uncomment what you
# need. The installed app ignores .env; values set in the real environment win over the file.

# Append start-up steps, the window's console and load errors to this file.
# LEMON_LOG=lemon.log

# (Chromium's sandbox can't be switched off from here: it starts before this file is read. On Linux
# machines where it won't start, run `pnpm dev --noSandbox`.)

# Open a saved document (.yjs) instead of a new file.
# LEMON_OPEN=test/fixtures/sample.yjs

# Send this prompt to the agent once the window is ready.
# LEMON_PROMPT=A landing page for a coffee shop in Lisbon

# Send that prompt to several agents: how many, and "split" (parts of one design) or "side" (a version each).
# LEMON_TEAM=3 split

# Save a picture of the window when the agent finishes (or after loading), then quit.
# LEMON_CAPTURE=capture.png

# Save a picture of the window after every agent step into this folder.
# LEMON_FILM=film
